# scCRS

**scCRS (Cytokine-response signature scoring for single-cell sequencing)** is a modular workflow for inferring cell-type-resolved cytokine-response programmes from scRNA-seq data and connecting those programmes to cell composition, T/B-cell states, B-cell regulatory networks, and Monocle3 pseudotime trajectories.

> **Research use only.** scCRS measures transcriptional similarity to a cytokine-response signature. It is not a cytokine concentration, receptor-occupancy measurement, or proof that a cytokine causally drives a cell state, regulatory edge, or differentiation process.

## Modules

| Question | Command / workflow | Main unit | Key output |
|---|---|---|---|
| Which cytokine-response programmes are present? | `sccrs-score` | patient × cell type | cytokine-response scores and coverage QC |
| Are scores associated with cell composition? | `sccrs-composition-association` | patient | Spearman/FDR correlation heatmap |
| Are scores associated with T/B states? | `sccrs-state-association`, `sccrs-state-scatter` | cell / patient × cell type | signed state scores and correlations |
| What candidate TF-target network accompanies a cytokine response in B-cell subsets? | `sccrs-bcell-network` | patient × B-cell subtype × group | prior-constrained TF-target edge tables and vector PDF |
| How does a response vary along B-cell differentiation? | `src/sccrs/r/scCRS_monocle3_cytokine_trajectory.R` | patient × pseudotime bin | UCell, GAM/PCRS and UMAP trajectory overlays |

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Xulab-collab/scCRS.git
cd scCRS
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate              # Linux/macOS
# .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1          # Windows PowerShell
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -e .
```

For the optional R modules, create an R 4.2+ environment and install `monocle3`, `Seurat`, `SingleCellExperiment`, `UCell`, `igraph`, `mgcv`, `dplyr`, `tidyr`, `ggplot2`, `patchwork`, `pheatmap`, `Cairo` and `optparse`; see [docs/installation.md](docs/installation.md).

## Input contract

### AnnData

An `.h5ad` object with cells in rows, genes in `var_names`, and `obs` columns for patient/sample and cell type. Optional `group` is required for group-specific networks. Use `--layer raw` only when `adata.raw` contains the intended RNA matrix; otherwise use an explicit layer or `X`.

### Cytokine dictionary

The standardized CSV has columns:

```text
cytokine,cell_type,gene,direction,weight
```

`direction` is `up` or `down`; `weight` is optional. The release includes `resources/Cytokine_Signatures_Human_All_CellTypes.csv`. Its response programmes are humanized signatures derived from the Immune Dictionary framework [Cui et al., Nature 2024](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06816-9). The originating perturbation data are publicly available as GEO GSE202186.

## End-to-end workflow

### 1. Prepare / score

```bash
sccrs-prepare-signatures --input Cytokine_Signatures_Human.xlsx --output signatures.csv

sccrs-score   --h5ad patient_pbmc.h5ad   --signatures resources/Cytokine_Signatures_Human_All_CellTypes.csv   --outdir results/scoring   --patient-col patient_id   --celltype-col cell_type   --celltype-map examples/pss_celltype_map_v2.csv   --layer raw

sccrs-add-group --h5ad patient_pbmc.h5ad --outdir results/scoring --patient-col patient_id --group-col group
sccrs-prepare-composition --h5ad patient_pbmc.h5ad --out results/scoring/patient_celltype_counts.csv --patient-col patient_id --celltype-col cell_type
```

### 2. Publication-ready response visualizations

Patient-level response heatmap (each cytokine is z-scored across patients; columns are annotated by group):

```bash
Rscript src/sccrs/r/scCRS_plot_patient_response_heatmap.R \
  --input results/scoring/patient_cytokine_scores_with_group.csv \
  --outdir results/patient_heatmap \
  --score-col overall_score_0_100 \
  --group-order "Normal,Non_High,High" \
  --cytokines "IFN-α1,IFN-β,IFN-γ,BAFF"
```

Cell-type-specific group comparison. The script produces one page per cytokine, with a violin, boxplot and patient points in every cell-type panel. It performs two-sided Wilcoxon tests for all group pairs and applies BH correction **within each cytokine × cell-type panel**.

```bash
Rscript src/sccrs/r/scCRS_plot_group_celltype_response.R \
  --input results/scoring/cell_type_cytokine_scores_with_group.csv \
  --outdir results/group_celltype_response \
  --score-col raw_rank_score \
  --group-order "Normal,Non_High,High" \
  --group-labels "Normal,Non-HGG,HGG" \
  --cell-types "B cells,CD4+ T,CD8+ T,NK,γδT,ILCs,myeloid cell,MAIT cells" \
  --cytokines "IFN-α1,IFN-β,IFN-γ,IFN-ε,IFN-κ,IFN-λ2"
```

The plotting scripts save the PDF and SVG-compatible vector graphics, the exact plotting data and the group-comparison statistics. Their input must contain the group column produced by `sccrs-add-group`.

### 3. Cell-proportion association

```bash
sccrs-composition-association   --patient-scores results/scoring/patient_cytokine_scores_with_group.csv   --celltype-counts results/scoring/patient_celltype_counts.csv   --outdir results/composition   --patient-score-col overall_score_0_100   --min-patients 5   --cytokine "IFN-α1,IFN-β,IFN-γ,BAFF"
```

### 3. T/B-cell-state association

```bash
sccrs-state-association   --h5ad patient_pbmc.h5ad   --cytokine-scores results/scoring/cell_type_cytokine_scores_with_group.csv   --state-signatures resources/scCRS_T_B_state_signatures.csv   --outdir results/state_association   --patient-col patient_id --celltype-col cell_type --layer raw

sccrs-state-scatter   --data results/state_association/state_cytokine_merged_data.csv   --outdir results/state_scatter   --cytokine "IFN-γ,BAFF"   --cell-type "Naive B cell,CD4+ T"   --state "plasmablast_differentiation"   --cytokine-score-col raw_rank_score
```

### 4. B-cell cytokine-response regulatory networks

Download a TF-target prior before running. A CollecTRI/DoRothEA high-confidence TSV is supported directly; cite both resources in downstream work.

```bash
sccrs-bcell-network   --h5ad Bcells_filtered.h5ad   --signatures resources/Cytokine_Signatures_Human_All_CellTypes.csv   --tf-target-prior regulatory_network_resources/CollecTRI_DoRothEA_A-C.tsv   --outdir results/bcell_network   --patient-col orig.ident --celltype-col cell_type --group-col group   --layer raw --signature-celltype B_cell   --min-cells 30 --min-patients 5 --min-abs-rho 0.50 --max-q 0.10   --make-pdf
```

Use `--pooled` to analyse all patients together. Use `--compare "Normal:HGG,Non-HGG:HGG"` for prespecified group comparisons. Network edges are *prior-supported, response-associated candidates*, not direct regulatory proof.

### 5. Monocle3 trajectory coupling

The R script expects a precomputed, ordered Monocle3 `cell_data_set` and does **not** rerun `learn_graph()` or `order_cells()`. Run it from the repository root:

```bash
Rscript src/sccrs/r/scCRS_monocle3_cytokine_trajectory.R   --cds Bcells_cds.rds --seurat Bcells_filtered.rds   --signatures resources/Cytokine_Signatures_Human_All_CellTypes.csv   --outdir results/bcell_trajectory   --celltype-col cell_type --patient-col orig.ident   --root-label "Naive B cell"   --branch1-name "Naive-to-IgA-plasma"   --branch1-label "IgA-secreting plasma cells"   --branch1-path-labels "Naive B cell,IFN-activated naive B cell,B_Transitional,resting naive B cell,IgA-secreting plasma cells"   --branch2-name "Naive-to-atypical-memory"   --branch2-label "atypical memory bcell"   --branch2-path-labels "Naive B cell,CD1C+ memory B,atypical memory bcell"   --signature-celltype B_cell   --vector-cytokines "IFN-α1,IFN-β,IFN-γ,IFN-ε,IFN-κ,IFN-λ2,BAFF,CD40L"
```

The trajectory module produces signed UCell scores per cell, patient × pseudotime-bin GAMs with patient random effect when feasible, PCRS, branch statistics, a response-associated branch overlay, and PDF/SVG maps. The arrow points toward the higher response end on the existing branch; it is **not** an RNA-velocity or causal-force vector.

## Outputs and reporting

Read [docs/outputs.md](docs/outputs.md) for exact tables. Report the input layer, patient/cell counts, signature coverage, cell-type mapping, thresholds, FDR, root and terminal labels, and the exact software version. Inspect coverage and sample counts before interpreting any score.

## Citation

Please cite the immune dictionary resource and the method resources used in your analysis:

- Cui A *et al.* Dictionary of immune responses to cytokines at single-cell resolution. *Nature* 625, 377–384 (2024). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06816-9
- Andreatta M & Carmona SJ. UCell: robust and scalable single-cell gene signature scoring. *Comput Struct Biotechnol J* 19, 3796–3798 (2021). https://doi.org/10.1016/j.csbj.2021.06.043
- Cao J *et al.* The single-cell transcriptional landscape of mammalian organogenesis. *Nature* 566, 496–502 (2019). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-0969-x
- Müller-Dott S *et al.* Expanding the coverage of regulons from high-confidence prior knowledge for accurate estimation of transcription factor activities. *Nucleic Acids Res* 51, 10934–10949 (2023). https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad841

## Repository hygiene

Do not commit `.h5ad`, Seurat/CDS files, raw counts, identifiable metadata, or downloaded large network databases. The provided `.gitignore` excludes typical analysis outputs and locally downloaded network priors.
